WEBVTT

c1
00:00:02.754 --> 00:00:07.474
In the previous video, I showed how turning the crank on this machine generates 20

c2
00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:11.954
different frequencies, also known as harmonics, which are turned into cosines here,

c3
00:00:11.954 --> 00:00:15.166
multiplied by coefficients. Then summed?

c4
00:00:15.618 --> 00:00:19.038
magnified and the resulting function plotted here on the front.

c5
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.374
This process is called synthesis.

c6
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.830
But this machine is called a harmonic analyzer.

c7
00:00:25.186 --> 00:00:29.106
which means it can be used to solve the much more difficult inverse problem called

c8
00:00:29.106 --> 00:00:33.986
analysis. For example, if I want to plot a particular function here, how do I set

c9
00:00:33.986 --> 00:00:36.158
the amplitude bars to produce it?

c10
00:00:36.546 --> 00:00:39.902
To illustrate how this machine does analysis, let's start with a square wave.

c11
00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.810
First, we use some unique properties of the square wave.

c12
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:49.214
Since it's periodic, And even.

c13
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:55.486
All of the information that function carries is contained in half a period.

c14
00:00:57.442 --> 00:00:59.198
So we'll take that half a period.

c15
00:00:59.522 --> 00:01:02.110
and sample to twenty equally spaced points.

c16
00:01:02.914 --> 00:01:06.270
We use the values of these points as the inputs for the machine.

c17
00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.378
When we turn the crank, we produce a new function that reveals the correct

c18
00:01:15.378 --> 00:01:19.474
coefficients. To see how we get these coefficients, we'll look at the side of the

c19
00:01:19.474 --> 00:01:24.542
machine. As I turn the crank, the tips of the rocker arms form a sinusoid.

c20
00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.838
The indices on the rocker arms run from high on the left to low on the right.

c21
00:01:32.226 --> 00:01:34.750
I'll flip the video to make it a little more intuitive.

c22
00:01:35.426 --> 00:01:39.186
When the rocker arm tips are lined up in a straight line, we'll call that crank

c23
00:01:39.186 --> 00:01:40.006
number zero.
